const passages = /* #__PURE__ */ JSON.parse("[{\"passageNumber\":1,\"title\":\"Suburban Commuter Rail Season Tickets & Civic Recycling Centers\",\"subtitle\":\"Public transport ticket schemes and municipal recycling guidelines\",\"text\":\"Section 1A: Regional Suburban Rail Season Ticket Guidelines\\nCommuters traveling regularly across the Greater Metropolitan Rail Network can save significantly by purchasing an Annual Gold Commuter Pass. An annual pass offers unlimited travel between designated origin and destination stations for fifty-two weeks for the price of forty individual weekly tickets. Passes can be loaded directly onto a reusable electronic SmartCard or issued as a secure digital barcode on the commuter railway mobile app.\\n\\nAnnual pass holders enjoy valuable supplementary privileges, including a complimentary thirty-three percent discount on off-peak leisure journeys across the entire national network for the holder and up to three accompanying adults. In the event of a lost SmartCard, cardholders must report the loss through the online passenger portal. A replacement card will be dispatched within three working days upon payment of a ten-pound administrative fee; all remaining pre-paid travel value is transferred to the replacement card automatically. Commuters changing employers or moving residence may apply for a pro-rata refund, provided at least four weeks of travel validity remain. Refunds are calculated based on the difference between the original purchase price and the cost of equivalent individual tickets for the period already used, minus a standard twenty-pound processing charge.\\n\\nSection 1B: Town Recycling and Household Waste Depot\\nThe Millbrook Municipal Household Waste Recycling Centre (HWRC) is open seven days a week, from eight in the morning until five in the evening, excluding Christmas Day and New Year's Day. The facility is free for local council taxpayers disposing of domestic household items in private passenger cars. Commercial traders, building contractors, and vehicles exceeding three point five tonnes gross weight must pre-register and pay commercial tipping fees by weight at the weighbridge office.\\n\\nTo ensure safety and maximize resource recovery, waste items must be pre-sorted prior to arrival. Dedicated disposal bays are provided for scrap metal, untreated timber, garden green waste, cardboard, car batteries, and household electricals. Waste engine oil must be poured into the specialized underground storage tank beside Bay Six; pouring oil into storm drains or standard waste skips is a criminal offense punishable by a fine of up to five thousand pounds. Children under twelve years of age and domestic pets must remain securely inside vehicles at all times while on site due to moving forklift machinery.\",\"wordCount\":420,\"questionGroups\":[{\"groupInstruction\":\"Do the following statements agree with the information given in Section 1A? In boxes 1–7 on your answer sheet, write:\\nTRUE if the statement agrees with the information\\nFALSE if the statement contradicts the information\\nNOT GIVEN if there is no information on this\",\"questionType\":\"true_false_not_given\",\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"g5-q1\",\"questionNumber\":1,\"type\":\"true_false_not_given\",\"topic\":\"transport\",\"estimatedBand\":5.5,\"prompt\":\"An Annual Gold Commuter Pass provides 52 weeks of travel for the price of 40 weekly tickets.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"TRUE\",\"explanation\":\"Section 1A states: 'fifty-two weeks for the price of forty individual weekly tickets.'\",\"evidence\":\"travel between designated origin and destination stations for fifty-two weeks for the price of forty individual weekly tickets.\"},{\"id\":\"g5-q2\",\"questionNumber\":2,\"type\":\"true_false_not_given\",\"topic\":\"transport\",\"estimatedBand\":6,\"prompt\":\"The off-peak discount extends to as many as three accompanying adults.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"TRUE\",\"explanation\":\"Section 1A states discount applies to the hold