ter opens at ____ in the morning.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"8\",\"eight\",\"8:00\"],\"explanation\":\"Section 1B states open from eight in the morning until five in the evening.\",\"evidence\":\"from eight in the morning until five in the evening\"},{\"id\":\"g5-q12\",\"questionNumber\":12,\"type\":\"sentence_completion\",\"topic\":\"commercial\",\"estimatedBand\":6.5,\"prompt\":\"Commercial fees are calculated by weight at the ____ office.\",\"correctAnswer\":\"weighbridge\",\"explanation\":\"Section 1B states commercial fees are paid by weight at the weighbridge office.\",\"evidence\":\"pay commercial tipping fees by weight at the weighbridge office.\"},{\"id\":\"g5-q13\",\"questionNumber\":13,\"type\":\"sentence_completion\",\"topic\":\"hazardous waste\",\"estimatedBand\":6.5,\"prompt\":\"Waste engine oil must be deposited in the underground tank next to Bay ____.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"Six\",\"6\"],\"explanation\":\"Section 1B indicates underground tank beside Bay Six.\",\"evidence\":\"underground storage tank beside Bay Six;\"},{\"id\":\"g5-q14\",\"questionNumber\":14,\"type\":\"sentence_completion\",\"topic\":\"penalties\",\"estimatedBand\":7,\"prompt\":\"Illegally dumping motor oil can incur a maximum fine of £____.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"5000\",\"5,000\",\"five thousand\"],\"explanation\":\"Section 1B states fine of up to five thousand pounds.\",\"evidence\":\"punishable by a fine of up to five thousand pounds.\"}]}]},{\"passageNumber\":2,\"title\":\"Workplace Parental Leave & Emergency First Aid Protocols\",\"subtitle\":\"Employee welfare directives and site health management at Clarion Tech\",\"text\":\"Section 2A: Enhanced Parental and Family Support Policy\\nClarion Tech recognizes the profound importance of supporting working parents. All permanent employees who have accrued at least twenty-six weeks of continuous service by the fifteenth week before the expected week of childbirth are eligible for our Enhanced Maternity and Paternity Leave. Eligible birthing mothers receive twenty-six weeks of fully paid maternity leave at one hundred percent of their base salary, followed by thirteen weeks at the statutory government rate. Non-birthing partners and secondary adoptive parents are entitled to six weeks of fully paid paternity and parental bonding leave, which may be taken consecutively or divided into two-week blocks within the child's first year.\\n\\nUpon returning to work, parents may request flexible working arrangements, such as compressed work weeks or core hour adjustments. The company also provides a phased return-to-work program, allowing returning mothers to work eighty percent of their contracted hours for the first three months while receiving one hundred percent of their salary. Furthermore, private nursing suites equipped with hospital-grade refrigeration units and ergonomic seating are available across all regional offices.\\n\\nSection 2B: Workplace First Aid and Fire Warden Responsibilities\\nTo maintain a safe working environment, Clarion Tech trains volunteer employees as Certified Workplace First Aiders and Floor Fire Wardens. Certified First Aiders receive an annual supplementary allowance of six hundred pounds and attend a mandatory refresher course every three years. Automated external defibrillators (AEDs) and first aid kits are mounted on every floor adjacent to the primary passenger lifts. In the event of a workplace medical emergency, employees must dial internal extension 4444 to dispatch the nearest first aider immediately.\\n\\nFloor Fire Wardens are responsible for orchestrating calm building evacuations during fire drills or alarm activations. Wardens must ensure all floor occupants exit via designated emergency stairwells; passenger lifts are automatically locked in the lobby during alarms and must never be used. Upon reaching the primary outdoor assembly point located in St. Peter's Square, wardens conduct roll calls using electronic tablet rosters. Employees must remain at the assembly point until the Chief Fire Safety Officer issues an official all-clear signal.\",\"wordCount\":400,\"questionGroups\":[{\"groupInstruction\":\"Complete the sentences below. Choose NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS AND/OR A NUMBER from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 15–21 on your answer sheet.\",\"questionType\":\"sentence_completion\",\"questions\":[{\"id\":\"g5-q15\",\"questionNumber\":15,\"type\":\"sentence_completion\",\"topic\":\"employment\",\"estimatedBand\":6,\"prompt\":\"Employees must have completed at least ____ weeks of continuous service to qualify for enhanced parental benefits.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"26\",\"twenty-six\"],\"explanation\":\"Section 2A states employees who accrued at least twenty-six weeks of continuous service.\",\"evidence\":\"accrued at least twenty-six weeks of continuous service\"},{\"id\":\"g5-q16\",\"questionNumber\":16,\"type\":\"sentence_completion\",\"topic\":\"maternity\",\"estimatedBand\":6,\"prompt\":\"Mothers receive ____ weeks of leave at full base salary.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"26\",\"twenty-six\"],\"explanation\":\"Section 2A states twenty-six weeks of fully paid maternity leave.\",\"evidence\":\"twenty-six weeks of fully paid maternity leave at one hundred percent of their base salary\"},{\"id\":\"g5-q17\",\"questionNumber\":17,\"type\":\"sentence_completion\",\"topic\":\"paternity\",\"estimatedBand\":6,\"prompt\":\"Non-birthing partners receive ____ weeks of fully paid leave.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"6\",\"six\"],\"explanation\":\"Section 2A states non-birthing partners receive six weeks of fully paid leave.\",\"evidence\":\"Non-birthing partners and secondary adoptive parents are entitled to six weeks of fully paid paternity\"},{\"id\":\"g5-q18\",\"questionNumber\":18,\"type\":\"sentence_completion\",\"topic\":\"welfare\",\"estimatedBand\":6.5,\"prompt\":\"Certified First Aiders receive an annual bonus payment of £____.\",\"correctAnswer\":[\"600\",\"six hundred\"],\"explanation\":\"Section 2B mentions